mode: "100644"
text: "# Video references and provenance\n\n## Source toolkits\n\nThe executable packages live in [`tools/video/`](../../../tools/video/README.md), separate from\nthe AGYOS runbooks that describe how to use them.\n\n## Prompt material\n\n| File | What it contains | Provenance status |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| [`nafay3d_style_prompts_recreated.md`](prompts/nafay3d_style_prompts_recreated.md) | Eight prompts newly written from publicly visible style descriptions, plus usage notes. | The file itself says these are not verbatim copies of the email-gated originals. Treat them as recreated prompts, not official source text. |\n| [`creator-motion-graphics-reference.txt`](prompts/creator-motion-graphics-reference.txt) | A supplied prompt and a long embedded HTML reference for the Creator Motion Graphics style. | The original filename was `Untitled document.txt`; its author and origin were not established. Treat it as an unverified reference dump. |\n\nThese documents describe the Nafay 3D motion-graphics presets. They are separate from the six\nanimation styles in the faceless-shorts toolkit and its own examples. Do not merge their style\nnames, models, or setup instructions. Claims in a prompt are source text, not independent\nverification that the referenced behavior or assets work.\n\nThe included package READMEs and any license notices are retained with the toolkits. The\nrecreated prompt file does not establish rights to the referenced style library, and the unverified\ndump does not establish rights to its embedded reference HTML. See\n[`tools/video/README.md`](../../../tools/video/README.md) for package-level licensing notes.\n"
